Dear all

An update on the compilation problems I reported here some time ago: I had tried to fit a multi-species occupancy model (with 334 species and 733 sites) with 5 chains run in parallel on a high-performance cluster, allocating each chain 10 GB of memory to run. And this model never wanted to end. It turns out that was too little memory. Thanks to Chris Paciorek's suggestions, we understood that it was somewhere in the buildMCMC() and the following compileNimble() step that the process gets stuck or slows down tremendously when it doesn't have enough memory. So increasing the amount of memory per chain from 10 to 20 GB/CPU solved the problem. Maybe this can be of help to other people who are experiencing similarly endless run times.

Thank you for your help, Chris!

Best wishes
Gesa

