Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

I have calculated open population survival estimates using CJS models in nimble, based on direct observation data, but I am stuck on how to create a spatial extension that incorporates sampling effort for each individual at each time step in order to make the model spatially explicit.

For a base model, without any covariates and with non-informative priors, I imagine I would need to edit the code below but I am not sure how exactly:

hmm.phitpt <- nimbleCode({
  delta[1] <- 1                    # Pr(alive t = 1) = 1
  delta[2] <- 0                    # Pr(dead t = 1) = 0
  for (t in 1:(T-1)){ # loop over time
    phi[t] ~ dunif(0, 1)           # prior survival
    gamma[1,1,t] <- phi[t]         # Pr(alive t -> alive t+1)
    gamma[1,2,t] <- 1 - phi[t]     # Pr(alive t -> dead t+1)
    gamma[2,1,t] <- 0              # Pr(dead t -> alive t+1)
    gamma[2,2,t] <- 1              # Pr(dead t -> dead t+1)
    p[t] ~ dunif(0, 1)             # prior detection
    omega[1,1,t] <- 1 - p[t]       # Pr(alive t -> non-detected t)
    omega[1,2,t] <- p[t]           # Pr(alive t -> detected t)
    omega[2,1,t] <- 1              # Pr(dead t -> non-detected t)
    omega[2,2,t] <- 0              # Pr(dead t -> detected t)
  }
  # likelihood
  for (i in 1:N){
    z[i,first[i]] ~ dcat(delta[1:2])
    for (j in (first[i]+1):T){
      z[i,j] ~ dcat(gamma[z[i,j-1], 1:2, j-1])
      y[i,j] ~ dcat(omega[z[i,j], 1:2, j-1])
    }
  }
})

I would greatly appreciate any support to help me build the code and on how to create a map from the same information.

With best regards,
Kennedy

