Hi Edel,

I've only taken a quick look at this, so I might be missing something, but when you say the "sample size of dirichlet-multinomial distribution is not sampled" are you referring to `n_lesle`?
If so, I see that `n_lesle` does not have a prior, hence NIMBLE does not assign an MCMC sampler to it. If you want it sampled, you'll need to give it a prior, so that NIMBLE considers it a parameter in the model.

-Chris

