Hi Edel,

if `n_p_migr` is defined by assignment (using `<-`) then it won't be sampled explicitly as a parameter in the model. However you should be able to monitor it if you want to, and the posterior samples of it will be determined completely (deterministically) from the posterior samples of `ro_dir`. Of course you can also just take the posterior samples of `ro_dir` and calculate `n_p_migr` for each sample.

Is `ro_dir` being sampled or is it staying at the same value during the course of the MCMC?

-chris

