That looks ok to me in terms of how to get the speed parameters that you want depending on the behavior (in-search vs. in-transit).

Another option is to have z[i,t] be Bernoulli and then grab the speed like this:

mean = mean.S*(1-z[i,t]) + mean.NS*z[i,t]

and similarly for `sd`.

