On Fri, Jul 28, 2023 at 7:29 AM Chris Paciorek <paci...@stat.berkeley.edu> wrote:
> Hi Rémy,
>
> If you provide some NAs for `y` via `data`, then those `y` elements will be treated as parameters.
>
> You generally will want to initialize such `y` elements to non-NA values via `inits`, though an MCMC will initialize them automatically if you do not do that. In other words you would have `y` in your `inits` list as well as in your `data` list, with the elements that are  NA in the `data` list filled in with actual values in `inits`. We have more information in the manual <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-building-models.html#missing-data-values>.
>
> -chris
>
